# Serialised corpus data is stored as ordinary Git objects rather than through Git LFS.
#
# The tracked contents of tf/ and xml/ occupy 599 MB on disk and compress to approximately
# 80 MB under the zlib and delta compression that Git applies by default. Git LFS stores every
# revision of every file whole and uncompressed, which is why the LFS object store in this
# repository had grown to 7.2 GB. The largest single file is 58 MB, which is within the 100 MB
# ceiling GitHub enforces on individual objects, so no file requires external storage.
#
# Cloning or pulling this repository therefore requires no additional tooling, authentication
# or bandwidth allowance. Declaring the serialised formats as text also ensures that line
# endings are preserved verbatim on platforms that would otherwise rewrite them.

*.tf    text eol=lf
*.tfx   text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf

*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.psd   binary
*.npy   binary
